A||N||8||Cplensdorf||Side Marker light screw color||||1||
Z||000000||Cplensdorf||02-24-2001||10:41 PM||||Can anyone tell me if the stock screws for the side marker lights on an 88GT are black (like my 86 SE) or clear (stainless/aluminum)?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Rodrv6||02-24-2001||10:44 PM||||Mine are black.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles :)||||reg||1
Z||000002||LZeitgeist||02-24-2001||10:46 PM||||Black. Anodized black.||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfiero||02-24-2001||10:59 PM||||They are "clear"......not black.  The black ones are for the interior stuff and have different heads.  It's possible that the early Fieros used different colored screws, but all of mine (including the 281 mile Formula) have plain stainless looking screws.<P>I have a TON of these, so LMK if you need any.||||reg||1
Z||000004||DaRkLoRD||02-25-2001||12:07 AM||||Get black, even if it wasn't stock for your year... the silver screws look cheap IMHO.. There's a guy I know with a beautiful 86 SE, and the trim screws on the fenders are silver... it looked like a Home Depot-brand repair job.. really stood out. yet apparently it came from the factory that way.<P>Personally I'd change them, or at least paint the heads black.<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||13
Z||000005||Cplensdorf||02-25-2001||09:08 AM||||Thanks, <BR>I too agree that the 'clear' ones look like a 'home-depot job'  The 88GT I just bought appears to be all original (all panels bear the correct matching VIN) with no accidents, but these screws make it look as though the marker lights were removed and replaced with the wrong screws.  My 86 SE has black ones.  Why the hell did they do that?||||reg||1
Z||000006||LZeitgeist||02-25-2001||10:31 AM||||Mine *look* silver-ish (in part) now, but that's from 13 years of weather and washings and wear. And I know they *used* to be black (on my 60K-mile Formula), because only the most-exposed areas of the screws have lightened.<P>Why in the heck would they put silver screws in otherwise completely-black trim? <p>[This message has been edited by LZeitgeist (edited 02-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||rogergarrison||02-25-2001||11:42 AM||||auto body supply shops have packets of all the right screws and fasteners for any part.||||reg||1
Z||000008||tgowens||02-25-2001||12:04 PM||||mrfiero is right on the head design.......and, they are torx head screws not regular screws -- the anodized aluminum screw with a slightly rounded head was used on the outside trim to help eliminate rusting against the metal clip on the fender under the marker trim. The black torx screws with the flat head were the interior screws.......they are, of course, interchangeable if you so desire.......||||reg||1
